# EXP 10 – Fine-Tuning for Domain Adaptation

## Objective

To demonstrate the process of domain adaptation by training a machine-learning model on domain-specific cybersecurity data and evaluating its performance on new cybersecurity-related queries.

## Problem Statement

A model trained on general-purpose data may not perform effectively when applied to a specialized domain. Domain adaptation helps improve the model's ability to understand and classify information related to a particular field.

The objective of this experiment is to demonstrate domain adaptation by first training a base classification model and then adapting it using cybersecurity-specific training data.

## Methodology

The experiment consists of the following steps:

1. Prepare general-purpose training data.
2. Train a base classification model.
3. Prepare cybersecurity-specific domain data.
4. Adapt the model using domain-specific data.
5. Test the adapted model with new cybersecurity queries.
6. Observe the domain-specific predictions.
